# ISA — SOP 4.3 Incident Notifications v2.0 (v0.9 model)

## Problem

SOP 4.3 v1.1 (effective 23 Dec 2025, endorsed COO) drives incident notifications from a 46-row matrix keyed on the current flat LIMSOC incident type codes (A01 to Z99) plus four cross-cutting "ZZZ" rows (any member injury, state resources, more than one club or service, potential media interest). The v0.9 Incident Categorisation proposal retires those codes in favour of an inheritance tree, Tags, Agency Status and Incident Outcome, so every row of the matrix loses its key.

The matrix also encodes three different things in one cell (whether a role is notified, under what condition, and whether they are expected to attend), and it silently assumes a recipient set is computed once from the type. The existing pager prototype (`lsv-notifications/Notifications_LSV_Final.xlsm`) confirms the current mechanism is stateless rule re-evaluation per event: an `Incident Type Updated` rule carries its own recipient list, so a type change pages a different set with no carry-forward and no de-duplication. Under v0.9, where Tags are added and removed and a Not Final type is refined to a child before closure, that gap becomes routine rather than occasional.

## Vision

An SOP a State Duty Officer can read once and apply under pressure: one page explains that an incident accumulates a subscription list (anyone qualified by any trigger stays on it), one table says which triggers qualify which role and what is expected of them, and one migration annex proves no current notification obligation was dropped. The senior manager of operations sees continuity of the roles they care about; the platform team sees a rules model LIMSOC can implement directly.

## Out of Scope

- Redesigning the categorisation model itself. The v0.9 pack is the source of truth; any gap it exposes (a missing Tag, an Outcome not gated) is fed back to the pack as a request, not changed here.
- The automated paging channel implementation (workbook, VBA, LIMSOC rules engine build). This SOP specifies the rules and the subscription behaviour the platform must support; it does not build them.
- SOP 4.4 Activity Logs and the Action Log design.
- Media and public communications procedures beyond the "potential media interest" trigger.
- The tag taxonomy as a whole (priority 1.8). Only the tags this SOP needs are named, and they are proposed to 1.8.

## Principles

- A notification obligation follows from what the incident is, what characterises it, how it ends and where it is, never from a code.
- Subscription is monotonic by default: qualifying is easy, leaving is deliberate.
- Notified and expected to attend are two different facts and are recorded separately.
- Every current obligation must be traceable to a new rule, and every new rule to a current obligation or a logged decision.

## Constraints

- v0.9 proposal pack is the model of record (tree, Type states, Tags, Outcome, Agency Status, precedence, Rule 1 to 4). Terminology must match it verbatim.
- Roles retained: LSV Comms Supervisor, Area Response Officer (ARO), Welfare and Peer Support, State Duty Officer, State Agency Commander, Chief Operating Officer, CEO, Lifesaving Lead (successor to Director Lifesaving Services). Senior Manager Operations is present in v1.1 and absent from Nick's list: fate to be decided, not silently dropped.
- Formal LSV SOP register and template (Scope, Audience, Responsibilities, Policy, Procedure, Special Considerations, Related Information, Abbreviations, Attachments, Revision, Endorsement). No conversational register.
- Australian English, no em dashes. Markdown source in workspace; OneDrive receives docx only, pushed with rclone copy.
- Plan first, then approval, then build. No SOP text drafted before Nick approves the plan.

## Goal

Produce SOP 4.3 v2.0 whose Procedure defines the per-incident subscription list and whose notification matrix is keyed on Type (with inheritance), Tags, Outcome and the agreed additional fields, with a migration annex mapping all 46 v1.1 matrix rows to new rules and a platform requirements annex for LIMSOC, verified against the v0.9 pack.

